{"nodes": [{"id": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_tests_reviewer_tests", "label": "reviewer-tests lane", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-tests.md", "source_location": "frontmatter name: reviewer-tests (model sonnet, effort high)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_tests_mutation_testing_in_scratch_worktree", "label": "Mutation testing in a scratch worktree", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-tests.md", "source_location": "lines 42-47, 62-66", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The question is not whether a test exists but whether it would fail if the code were wrong, and the only way to settle that is to break the code and run the test. The mutation happens in a scratch worktree \u2014 an exact copy on a detached commit not on any branch \u2014 which the lead discards whole, so the mutation is left in place and there is no cleanup and no risk to the reviewed tree. Where no scratch path was given, the reviewer records `mutation testing: unavailable` rather than improvising a mutation elsewhere."}, {"id": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_tests_primary_working_tree_immutability", "label": "Primary working tree immutability and the lead's digest check", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-tests.md", "source_location": "lines 51-60", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Concurrent lanes read the primary tree and the lead commits it, so a write there means the diff that ships is not the diff that was reviewed. The lead takes a content digest before spawning reviewers and compares after they drain, which detects a write and costs the round a rerun \u2014 but the stated reason not to write is that it corrupts the review, not that it would be caught. The digest checks the result rather than enumerating causes, because no permission list catches every spelling."}], "edges": [{"source": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_tests_reviewer_tests", "target": "user__claude_skills_dev_loop_references_review_lanes_review_lanes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-tests.md", "source_location": "line 37", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_tests_reviewer_tests", "target": "user__claude_skills_dev_loop_skill_dev_loop", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-tests.md", "source_location": "description; lines 48-49", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_tests_reviewer_tests", "target": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_architecture_lane_ownership_boundary", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-tests.md", "source_location": "lines 70-71", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_tests_reviewer_tests", "target": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_architecture_empty_findings_is_valid", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-tests.md", "source_location": "lines 77-78", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_tests_reviewer_tests", "target": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_architecture_evidence_and_cause_honesty", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-tests.md", "source_location": "lines 72-76", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_tests_reviewer_tests", "target": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_tests_mutation_testing_in_scratch_worktree", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-tests.md",